{
  "note": [
    "A census of the live Base Sepolia diamond, read off the chain on 31 August 2026",
    "and committed as DATA so that test/AppealDepositSoftRefundUpgrade.t.sol has an",
    "expected side that does NOT come from the script it is checking.",
    "",
    "Why this file exists at all. script/UpgradeAppealDepositSoftRefund.s.sol files all",
    "fifty-nine ArbiterRegistryFacet selectors under Replace and none under Add. Replace",
    "reverts on a selector that is not mounted and Add reverts on one that is, so a single",
    "selector in the wrong group drops the WHOLE diamondCut in one transaction, after the",
    "facet has already been paid for. A bench that asked the script's own replaceSelectors()",
    "what is mounted would agree with the script no matter which group anything was filed",
    "under. That is the fourth way to be fooled by a measurement and it cost a whole cut on",
    "16 August 2026. So the question 'is each of these mounted today' is answered here, by",
    "the chain, and the script only supplies the actual side.",
    "",
    "count is 221 and not 222: notifyWorkHandedIn() (0x3af384eb) is NOT mounted yet -- it",
    "arrives with script/UpgradeRegistryHandInSignal.s.sol, a different cut on a different",
    "facet. This cut neither needs it nor is disturbed by it, which is why the two are",
    "order-independent.",
    "",
    "arbiterRegistryCount is 59 and equals what out/ArbiterRegistryFacet.sol compiles to,",
    "which is what makes 'no Add group' a true claim rather than a hope.",
    "",
    "arbiterRegistryCodeSize is the size of the code running TODAY. The tree compiles to",
    "24367. The two differing is what says there is something to ship; the two agreeing",
    "after the cut is what says the new code is really running, because the selector count",
    "cannot say it -- it is identical on both sides of a pure Replace."
  ],
